A SAMPLE registry, not a real one. The registry repo doesn't exist yet.

The portal pages under /skills/ are built from this folder until it does. While this file is here,
every portal page says it shows sample skills that can't be installed, and asks search engines not
to index it.

It holds what the registry publishes, in the formats of docs/REGISTRY-FORMAT.md: index.json,
revocations.json and recipes/<sha256>.yaml with each one's .sig. All publishers are made up
(example-*), and every host is under example.com, example.net or example.org. The first three
recipes are the signed example from docs/examples/registry; the others were signed with throwaway
keys, whose private halves were deleted. The index and revocations.json are left unsigned, as the
portal doesn't read their signatures: Tux checks those itself and never trusts the site.

To build the portal from a real registry, point REGISTRY_DIR at a folder with the same layout,
without this file:

    REGISTRY_DIR=/path/to/published python3 build.py
